  "caption": "Quinn's first weeks on the tools: knees grumbling from kneeling, shoulders sulking after a day of overhead work.\n\nYears of the same physical tasks, big-day load spikes and no off-season can build fatigue faster than strength, so aches often creep in.\n\nWhat can help: two short strength sessions a week for legs, back, shoulders and trunk, a five-minute warm-up before the first heavy lift, letting knee pads, trolleys and lifting aids (or a mate) share the load, rotating tasks, and taking proper rest when your body complains.\n\nIf aches keep coming back, follow a pattern or keep building, get them looked at early rather than pushing through. Sudden or severe symptoms need urgent medical care.\n\nOur Sydney CBD and Chatswood physios can help. Book via the link in bio.\n\nGeneral information only — not a substitute for an individual assessment.",
